## 3. Database Schema Implementation Plan

We will create Mongoose models matching Document 8 exactly:

1. **`User`**: Base record containing unique indexed `phone` (with regex `/^[6-9]\d{9}$/`), sparse unique `email`, `role`, verification statuses, login lock parameters (`loginAttempts`, `lockUntil`), and FCM tokens.
2. **`OtpSession`**: OTP phone verification session. Uses MongoDB TTL index on `expiresAt` set to 10 minutes. Plaintext OTP is stored hashed with `bcrypt`.
3. **`Customer`**: 1:1 extends `User`. Contains `walletBalance` in paise, `loyaltyCoins`, `membershipPlan`, and unique `referralCode`.
4. **`Professional`**: 1:1 extends `User`. Stores 2dsphere indexes for `currentLocation` and `homeAddress.coordinates`. Stores status transitions, rating averages, bank details, and Razorpay payouts meta.
5. **`ProfessionalDocuments`**: Stored separately. Holds document status and URLs for KYC (Aadhaar, PAN, certificates, police check). Verified status, reviewed timestamps.
6. **`ProfessionalAvailability`**: Weekly schedule tracking (active days, start/end hours, breaks), blocked dates, and override options.
7. **`City`** & **`Zone`**: Geographic zones for service boundaries. Zones contain GeoJSON polygons and dynamic `pricingMultiplier` / `surgeMultiplier`.
8. **`Category`**, **`Service`**, **`ServicePackage`**, and **`ServiceAddon`**: Complete catalogue structure.
   - Pricing fields in Mongoose packages/addons are strict integers representing paise.
9. **`Address`**: GeoJSON Point coordinates, links to resolved `zoneId`. Limit of 5 addresses per customer.
10. **`Booking`**: Booking number formatted as `SP + YYMMDD + 4-digit sequence`. Deeply nested snapshots of `serviceAddressSnapshot` and `pricing` structure (frozen at the moment of booking creation). Stores start/complete OTP hashes (bcrypt).
11. **`Payment`**: Connects Razorpay Order IDs, capturing transaction signatures and raw webhook log history.
12. **`Review`**: Individual review per booking rating the professional and service overall, triggering real-time atomic updates of ratings on both professionals and services.
13. **`Coupon`** & **`CouponUsage`**: Flat or percentage promo codes. Enforces scope exclusions (city/service limits) and first-booking constraints.
14. **`Wallet`** & **`WalletTransaction`**: Tracks credits/debits in paise (e.g. referral rewards, booking refunds).
15. **`Payouts`** (or `ProfessionalPayout`): Weekly payouts settling COMPLETED booking totals to professionals.
16. **`SupportTicket`**: Message logs, assigned support admin, SLA deadlines, and breach markers.
17. **`Notification`**: Channel delivery records (push, WhatsApp, SMS, email) and read receipts.
18. **`LocationHistory`**: Coordinates log for professionals in transit.
19. **`SafetyIncident`**: Critical reports and panic button/SOS trigger logs.
20. **`AuditLog`**: Read-only ledger throwing errors on updates/deletes with auto-redaction of PII.
21. **`AnalyticsEvent`**: Batch-ingestion schema for system telemetry.

